{"kind":"assert","text":"C3 ruling on b4e00d0a: send and settle give one status for one record.\n\n1. `settledOfSent` gives `recorded` for a kept `folded` outcome when\n   the record's phase is `accepted`. It gives `unknown` when the phase\n   is `mismatch`. Read the phase of `sent.record`. Change nothing else\n   in the function. `lost` and `archivedSettlement` stay `unknown`.\n2. Authority. This grants nothing new. `settledOf` already gives\n   `recorded` for the phase `accepted`, and `Custody.folded` sets that\n   phase only when the folded intent is a signing of the record. The\n   phase is the one fact both paths read. Today the two paths differ\n   on the same stored record, and a page would show `unknown` after a\n   repeated send and `recorded` after a read.\n3. My ruling 72496543 said in item 1 that this layer reads a folded\n   record as `unknown`. That was true of `settledOfSent` alone. Item 4\n   stands as written, for both paths. Item 1 stands for `unsent`.\n4. Cases. The late-fold case keeps both assertions: `settle` and the\n   repeated `send` give `recorded`. Add one case: a fold whose intent\n   is no signing of the record gives `unknown` through both paths.\n   Name the existing case instead when one shows that already.\n5. The fixture clock repair is yours. Use the existing `sendableAt`\n   margin. Change no death rule.\n\nThe control of 72496543 stays as proposed. No status, no page copy\nand no stored layout changes. The stronger cause still waits for C4\nand E3. Run the two checks of 7fe68ffe at the new head.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}